# Own-wording spells of Grim Hollow Player's Guide (2024), chunk 1 (first 51 names alphabetically). TEXT = {name: [summary, full]}.
TEXT = {
"Arboreal Curse": ["Range 60 ft. Constitution save or Restrained as flesh turns to bark. Three failed saves turn the target into a tree (Petrified).",
 "Range 60 ft. You try to turn one creature you can see into wood. The target makes a Constitution save. On a fail it has the Restrained condition as bark spreads over its flesh. On a success its Speed is 0 until the start of your next turn.\n\n**Repeating saves.** A creature Restrained by this spell makes a Constitution save at the end of each of its turns. Three successes end the condition. Three failures turn it into a tree and it has the Petrified condition. The saves need not be consecutive. Keep a separate count of successes and failures until one count reaches three.\n\n**Lasting harm.** If the creature is burned, chopped down or otherwise destroyed while Petrified, it dies. The change lasts until reversed within 1 year by Greater Restoration, Wish or similar magic. If the creature stays a tree for 1 year and 1 day, the change becomes permanent and nothing can restore its original form."],
"Arcane Aegis": ["You gain 2d10 Temporary Hit Points. Melee attackers who hit you take Force damage equal to the Temporary Hit Points they remove. +2d10 per slot level above 1.",
 "Self, 1 minute. A shimmering light surrounds you, then fades. You gain 2d10 Temporary Hit Points. If a creature hits you with a melee attack before the spell ends, it takes Force damage equal to the number of Temporary Hit Points that attack removed from you. The spell ends early when you have no Temporary Hit Points left.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** You gain an extra 2d10 Temporary Hit Points for each slot level above 1."],
"Assisted Aim": ["Up to 3 creatures within 30 ft get +1 to Ranged weapon attack rolls and double weapon range for 1 minute. +1 target per slot level above 1.",
 "Range 30 ft, 1 minute. You sharpen the aim of up to three creatures within range. Each target gains a +1 bonus to attack rolls made with Ranged weapons. The normal and long range of Ranged weapons a target wields are also doubled for the duration.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** You can target one more creature for each slot level above 1."],
"Binding Pledge": ["Ritual. Know at once when a willing creature breaks its promise, oath or contract, then track its distance and direction. 10 days.",
 "Touch, 10 days, ritual. A willing creature within range makes a promise, swears an oath or enters a contract. For the duration you know at once if it breaks that promise, oath or contract. When that happens, you know the creature's distance and direction for the rest of the duration. If the spell is dispelled, you know it immediately but do not learn the creature's distance and direction.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** With a level 3 or 4 slot the duration is 30 days. With a level 5 or 6 slot it is 1 year. With a level 7 or higher slot it lasts until dispelled."],
"Bloat": ["Range 30 ft. Constitution save, 3d10 Necrotic (half on success). Damage equal to or above its Constitution score makes the target float 5 ft.",
 "Range 30 ft, 1 round. You make the gases inside a creature you can see swell. The target makes a Constitution save and takes 3d10 Necrotic damage on a fail, or half as much on a success.\n\n**Floating.** If the damage the creature takes equals or exceeds its Constitution score, it floats 5 feet straight up and stays suspended until the start of your next turn. It can only move by pushing or pulling on a fixed object or surface within reach, such as a wall or ceiling, and moves as if climbing. When the spell ends, it drifts gently to the ground."],
"Blood Bond": ["Spend 3 Hit Point Dice. Target gains Temporary Hit Points equal to the roll, and you share a telepathic link and sense of direction for 1 hour.",
 "Touch, 1 hour. To cast this spell you must expend three Hit Point Dice, or it fails automatically. Roll the expended dice. The target gains Temporary Hit Points equal to the total.\n\n**Link.** For the duration you know the target's direction and distance, and you and the target can speak telepathically. You can also target that creature with a spell that has a range of Self or Touch, no matter the distance between you. These benefits are suppressed while you are on different planes.\n\n**Breaking the bond.** The target can end the spell early at any time. If it does, it loses any remaining Temporary Hit Points from this spell and takes Necrotic damage equal to the Temporary Hit Points lost.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** With a level 5 or 6 slot the duration is 8 hours. With a level 7 or 8 slot it is 24 hours. With a level 9 slot it is 7 days."],
"Blood Rush": ["Bonus Action, spend 1 Hit Point Die. Roll it twice and regain that total plus your spellcasting modifier in Hit Points. +1 die per slot level above 1.",
 "Self, Bonus Action. To cast this spell you must expend one Hit Point Die, or it fails automatically. Roll that Hit Point Die twice and add the results. You regain Hit Points equal to that total plus your spellcasting ability modifier.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** You can expend one more Hit Point Die for each slot level above 1."],
"Blood Tide": ["Spend 6 Hit Point Dice. 100 ft by 10 ft Line, Dexterity save. Fail: pushed 100 ft, Prone, Bludgeoning damage equal to a roll of the spent dice plus your modifier. Half on success.",
 "Self (100-foot Line), Action. To cast this spell you must expend six Hit Point Dice, or it fails automatically. A gout of blood blasts out from you in a Line 100 feet long and 10 feet wide, in a direction you choose. Each creature in the Line makes a Dexterity save.\n\n**Failed save.** The creature is pushed 100 feet along the Line away from you, has the Prone condition, and takes Bludgeoning damage equal to a roll of the Hit Point Dice you expended plus your spellcasting ability modifier.\n\n**Successful save.** The creature takes half as much damage only.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** You can expend one more Hit Point Die for each slot level above 6."],
"Blood Wisp": ["Spend 2 Hit Point Dice. A red wisp circles you and lets you reroll one damage die on your spells, but it takes that damage. 1 hour.",
 "Self, 1 hour. Material cost: a ruby worth 10 GP. To cast this spell you must expend two Hit Point Dice, or it fails automatically. Roll the expended dice. You create a red wisp whose Hit Points equal the roll plus your spellcasting ability modifier. It circles your head, has an AC of 10 plus your spellcasting ability modifier, and uses your saving throws.\n\n**Rerolls.** Each time you roll damage for a spell while the wisp circles you, you can reroll one of the damage dice. You must use the new roll, and the wisp takes damage equal to that new roll. If the wisp drops to 0 Hit Points, the spell ends.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** You can expend one more Hit Point Die for each slot level above 2."],
"Bloodbane Rune": ["Spend 1 Hit Point Die. Weapon glows near Undead (30 ft) and once per turn deals extra Radiant damage equal to a roll of the spent dice. Concentration, 1 minute.",
 "Touch, Concentration up to 1 minute. To cast this spell you must expend one Hit Point Die, or it fails automatically. You draw a rune in blood on a weapon of your choice within range. While you wield it for the duration, the weapon weeps a phantasmal red ichor whenever it is within 30 feet of an Undead creature. Once per turn, when you damage an Undead creature with the weapon, you deal extra Radiant damage. Roll the number of Hit Point Dice you expended to cast the spell to find that damage.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** You expend one more Hit Point Die for each slot level above 1. With a level 2 slot, Concentration can last up to 10 minutes. With a level 3 or higher slot, up to 1 hour."],
"Bloodletter": ["Bonus Action. Nonmagical weapon: the first creature hit makes a Constitution save or gets a festering wound taking 2d6 Necrotic at the start of each turn. +1d6 per slot level above 2.",
 "Touch, Bonus Action, Concentration up to 1 minute. You touch a nonmagical weapon. Until the spell ends, the first creature the weapon hits must succeed on a Constitution save or gain a festering wound. A creature with a festering wound takes 2d6 Necrotic damage at the start of each of its turns for the duration. A creature can have only one festering wound at a time. If the creature receives healing, the spell and the recurring damage end.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** The damage increases by 1d6 for each slot level above 2."],
"Boil Blood": ["Spend 1 Hit Point Die. A willing target takes Fire damage equal to a roll of the spent die, and its Poisoned condition ends.",
 "Touch. To cast this spell you must expend one Hit Point Die, or it fails automatically. A willing target takes Fire damage equal to a roll of the expended Hit Point Die. If the target has the Poisoned condition, that condition ends at once."],
"Burst Forth": ["Spend 7 Hit Point Dice. Range 200 ft. Teleport inside a creature and burst out. Constitution save, Necrotic damage equal to a roll of the spent dice plus your modifier (half on success).",
 "Range 200 ft. To cast this spell you must expend seven Hit Point Dice, or it fails automatically. You teleport inside a creature you can see within range and burst out of it in a spray of gore, landing in the nearest unoccupied space. The target makes a Constitution save. It takes Necrotic damage equal to a roll of the Hit Point Dice you expended plus your spellcasting ability modifier on a fail, or half as much on a success.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** You can expend one more Hit Point Die for each slot level above 7."],
"Call the Rabid Beast": ["Touch. Target gets 20 Temporary Hit Points, AC 17 minimum, +5 Strength damage, a 1d6 Bite, Frightened immunity. DC 10 Wisdom save each turn or it loses control.",
 "Touch, Concentration up to 1 minute. A creature you touch becomes a rabid monster full of primal fury. It grows thick fur and a fanged maw, and gains 20 Temporary Hit Points. While transformed it has these effects:\n- Its AC is 17 if its AC is lower than that.\n- It gets a +5 bonus to damage rolls with Strength-based attacks.\n- It can make a Bite attack as a Bonus Action. The Bite deals 1d6 plus its Strength modifier Slashing damage.\n- It is immune to the Frightened condition.\n- It cannot cast spells or maintain Concentration.\n\n**Loss of control.** At the start of each of its turns, the creature must succeed on a DC 10 Wisdom save or lose control until the spell ends. A creature that has lost control must take the Attack action on each of its turns, using melee attacks against the nearest creature. If none is within reach, it must use its movement, and the Dash action if needed, to move toward the nearest creature."],
"Calling Card": ["Cantrip. Touch a corpse to leave a visible or Invisible magical mark. Anyone who takes the Study action on the corpse finds it automatically. Lasts until dispelled.",
 "Touch, until dispelled. You touch a corpse and leave a magical mark on it. You choose whether the mark is visible, appearing as a rune or word written on the flesh, or Invisible. A creature that takes the Study action to examine the corpse specifically detects the mark automatically, whether it is visible or Invisible."],
"Chains of Beleth": ["Range 100 ft. 20-ft Sphere of barbed chains. Dexterity save: 8d6 Piercing and Restrained. Restrained creatures take 3d6 Bludgeoning at turn end. +1d6 per slot level above 6.",
 "Range 100 ft, Concentration up to 1 minute. Barbed chains ending in meat hooks burst from the ground at a point you can see within range and flail about in a Sphere of 20-foot radius centered there. Each creature in the area makes a Dexterity save. On a fail it takes 8d6 Piercing damage and has the Restrained condition until the spell ends.\n\n**Entering the area.** The first time a creature enters the area on a turn, or starts its turn there, it must succeed on a Dexterity save or have the Restrained condition while in the area or until it breaks free.\n\n**Breaking free.** A creature Restrained by the chains can take an action to make a Strength (Athletics) check against your spell save DC. On a success it is no longer Restrained.\n\n**Ongoing damage.** When a creature Restrained by this spell ends its turn, it takes 3d6 Bludgeoning damage.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** The initial and later damage both increase by 1d6 for each slot level above 6."],
"Circle of Scarlet": ["Spend 4 Hit Point Dice. Range 120 ft. 20-ft radius, 100-ft high Cylinder. Constitution save, Necrotic damage equal to a roll of the spent dice plus your modifier (half on success). You gain 10 Temporary Hit Points per creature that fails.",
 "Range 120 ft. To cast this spell you must expend four Hit Point Dice, or it fails automatically. A crimson pillar erupts from the ground in a Cylinder of 20-foot radius and 100-foot height centered on a point within range. Each creature in the Cylinder makes a Constitution save. On a fail it takes Necrotic damage equal to a roll of the Hit Point Dice you expended plus your spellcasting ability modifier. On a success it takes half as much.\n\n**Feeding.** For each creature that fails the save, you gain 10 Temporary Hit Points."],
"Conjure Plants": ["Range 60 ft. A Large mass of vines (10 minutes) that shields you and can move 30 ft. Creatures near it make a Dexterity save or take 3d6 Slashing. +1d6 per slot level above 3.",
 "Range 60 ft, Concentration up to 10 minutes. You conjure a Large mass of animated vines, stems, shoots, roots and leaves in an unoccupied space you can see within range. It lasts for the duration.\n\n**Cover.** While you are within 5 feet of the plants or share a space with them, you count as being in a Lightly Obscured area. Other creatures cannot enter the plants' space.\n\n**Moving.** When you move on your turn, you can also move the plants up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see.\n\n**Lashing out.** Whenever the plants move within 5 feet of a creature you can see, or a creature you can see enters a space within 5 feet of them or ends its turn there, you can force that creature to make a Dexterity save. On a fail it takes 3d6 Slashing damage. A creature makes this save only once per turn.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** The damage increases by 1d6 for each slot level above 3."],
"Consume Mind": ["Eat the brain of a creature dead 3 days or less to recall its memories for 1 hour. Recall with a Magic action and a spellcasting check against DC equal to its Intelligence score.",
 "Self, 1 hour. Material: a 1-ounce piece of fresh or magically preserved brain from another creature. You consume the brain of a dead creature and gain access to its memories. The creature must have a brain and cannot be Undead. The spell fails if the creature has been dead and unpreserved for more than 3 days.\n\n**Recalling.** Until the spell ends, you can try to recall a memory, such as family history, recent events, building layouts, passwords or details of the creature's death. To do so, take a Magic action and make an ability check using your spellcasting ability modifier. The DC equals the corpse's Intelligence score. After you take a Magic action to recall a piece of information, you cannot try to recall that same piece again."],
"Consumption": ["Spend 1 Hit Point Die. Range 60 ft. Target takes Necrotic damage equal to a roll of the spent die and repeats it on each failed Constitution save at turn end. +1 target per slot level above 1.",
 "Range 60 ft, Concentration up to 1 minute. To cast this spell you must expend one Hit Point Die, or it fails automatically. Choose a creature within range and roll the expended die. The target takes Necrotic damage equal to the result. At the end of each of its turns while the spell lasts, the target makes a Constitution save. On a fail it takes that damage again. On a success the spell ends.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** You can target one more creature for each slot level above 1."],
"Creeping Death": ["Spend 8 Hit Point Dice. Range 60 ft. Target dies if its Hit Points fall to or below a threshold set by your roll. Raise the threshold with Constitution saves. Concentration, 1 minute.",
 "Range 60 ft, Concentration up to 1 minute. To cast this spell you must expend eight Hit Point Dice, or it fails automatically. Roll the expended dice. The total is the target's Creeping Death threshold. For the duration, if the creature's Hit Points are reduced to its Creeping Death threshold or lower, it dies at once.\n\n**Pushing the threshold.** As a Bonus Action, you can force the target to make a Constitution save. On a fail, roll 2d6 and add the result to the threshold. On a success, add half the result instead. If the creature succeeds on three of these saves, which need not be consecutive, the spell ends early."],
"Creeping Touch": ["Detach your hand as a Spider for 10 minutes. Telepathy within 100 ft and see through its eyes with a Magic action. If it dies or fails to return, you take 1d6 Psychic damage.",
 "Self, Concentration up to 10 minutes. You detach your hand at the wrist and turn it into a Spider. While the spider is within 100 feet of you, you can speak with it telepathically. As a Magic action you can see through its eyes and hear what it hears until the start of your next turn. During that time you are unaware of your own surroundings.\n\n**Ending.** As a Bonus Action you can command the spider to return to you. When it arrives, it reattaches as your hand and the spell ends. If the spider is killed or does not return before the spell ends, your hand is restored but you take 1d6 Psychic damage."],
"Crimson Lash": ["Spend 1 Hit Point Die. Blood lash is a Simple weapon (Light, Finesse, Reach), uses your spellcasting modifier, deals Necrotic damage of the spent die size, and lowers Hit Point maximum by the damage dealt. 1 minute.",
 "Self, 1 minute. To cast this spell you must expend one Hit Point Die, or it fails automatically. A writhing lash of coagulated blood springs from your hand. It has these properties:\n- It counts as a Simple weapon and you are proficient with it.\n- It has the Light, Finesse and Reach properties.\n- You can use your spellcasting ability modifier instead of Strength or Dexterity for attack and damage rolls with it.\n- Its damage die matches the Hit Point Die you expended, and its damage is Necrotic.\n- Each time a creature takes damage from the lash, its Hit Point maximum decreases by the damage taken.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** With a level 3 or 4 slot, you can make two attacks with the lash when you take the Attack action. With a level 5 or higher slot, you can make three."],
"Crown of Radiance": ["Self, 10 minutes. A Fiend, Fey or Undead within 30 ft of you takes 2d8 Radiant damage when it moves there or starts its turn there. Sheds Bright Light 30 ft, Dim Light 30 ft more.",
 "Self, 10 minutes. A flaming crown of holy light settles on your head until the spell ends. A Fiend, Fey or Undead that moves within 30 feet of you, or starts its turn within 30 feet of you, takes 2d8 Radiant damage. The crown sheds Bright Light in a 30-foot radius and Dim Light for another 30 feet."],
"Curse of Conceited Obsession": ["Level 6 staged curse. Charisma save: 8d10 Psychic and cursed on a fail, 4d6 on a success. Stages bring self-admiration, Advantage against the target, then Disadvantage on attacks. Ends as a Weeping Willow.",
 "Unlimited range, until cured. Material cost: a thread from the target's bed or clothes, a handful of teeth and a gilded mirror worth 1,000+ GP, all consumed. You curse a creature with obsessive self-infatuation. The target makes a Charisma save.\n\n**Successful save.** The target takes 4d6 Psychic damage and knows it was cursed. For 1 minute it also takes 1d6 Psychic damage at the start of each of its turns.\n\n**Failed save.** The target takes 8d10 Psychic damage and is cursed.\n\n**Trigger.** The next time the cursed creature looks into a mirror or reflective surface, the surface cracks or warps and the curse moves to Stage 1.\n\n**Stage 1.** It must stop and admire itself whenever it sees its reflection and fusses constantly over its looks.\n\n**Stage 2.** It becomes obsessed with finding its reflection everywhere, even in foes' eyes. Attacks against it have Advantage.\n\n**Stage 3.** It feels driven to find or build a place where it can see itself from many angles, and it must stay there admiring itself. It also has Disadvantage on attack rolls.\n\n**Culmination.** The creature twists into a deformed figure and becomes a Weeping Willow."],
"Curse of Crushing Sensation": ["Level 6 staged curse. Constitution save: 8d10 Thunder and cursed on a fail, 4d6 on a success. Stages bring sensory aversion, Thunder Vulnerability and no armor, then Vulnerability to all damage but Psychic outside a lair. Ends as a Sightless Agony.",
 "Unlimited range, until cured. Material cost: a drop of the target's blood, a shred of silk and a horn worth 1,000+ GP, all consumed. You curse a creature with painful hypersensitivity. The target makes a Constitution save.\n\n**Successful save.** The target takes 4d6 Thunder damage and knows it was cursed. For 1 minute it also takes 1d6 Thunder damage at the start of each of its turns.\n\n**Failed save.** The target takes 8d10 Thunder damage and is cursed.\n\n**Trigger.** The next time the target hears a loud noise, it gets a crippling headache and the curse moves to Stage 1.\n\n**Stage 1.** It avoids Bright Light, loud noises and extreme temperatures, and dislikes being touched.\n\n**Stage 2.** It cannot bear rough or heavy clothing and cannot wear armor. It has Vulnerability to Thunder damage. It also has Disadvantage on attack rolls if it or its target is in an area of Bright Light.\n\n**Stage 3.** Even mild sensation is intolerable. It feels driven to find a dark, quiet lair such as a deep cave or dungeon and cannot willingly leave it. While outside its lair it has Vulnerability to all damage except Psychic.\n\n**Culmination.** The creature twists into a deformed figure and becomes a Sightless Agony."],
"Curse of Damned Aging": ["Level 4 staged curse. Strength save: 6d10 Necrotic and cursed on a fail, 2d10 on a success. Stages bring lethargy, only 25 percent of Hit Point Dice usable on a Short Rest, then Disadvantage on Strength, Dexterity and Constitution saves. Ends as a Body Snatcher.",
 "Unlimited range, until cured. Material cost: a childhood possession of the target, a pint of blood and a watch worth 600+ GP, all consumed. You curse a creature with horrific aging. The target makes a Strength save.\n\n**Successful save.** The target takes 2d10 Necrotic damage and knows it was cursed. For 1 minute it has Vulnerability to Bludgeoning, Piercing or Slashing damage, chosen by you when you cast the spell.\n\n**Failed save.** The target takes 6d10 Necrotic damage and is cursed.\n\n**Trigger.** When the target next finishes a Long Rest, it finds new wrinkles, grey hairs or spots, and the curse moves to Stage 1.\n\n**Stage 1.** It feels compelled to rest whenever it can and becomes lethargic and lazy.\n\n**Stage 2.** It becomes feeble. After a Short Rest it can use only 25 percent of its Hit Point Dice (rounded up) to regain Hit Points.\n\n**Stage 3.** It ages rapidly and grows decrepit. It has Disadvantage on Strength, Dexterity and Constitution saves.\n\n**Culmination.** The creature twists into a deformed figure and becomes a Body Snatcher."],
"Curse of Fastidious Pride": ["Level 3 staged curse. Intelligence save: 4d10 Psychic, Blinded 1 minute and cursed on a fail, 2d10 on a success. Stages bring paranoia, no Short Rest benefit, then Disadvantage after a failed D20 Test. Ends as a Mind Siphon.",
 "Unlimited range, until cured. Material cost: a shred of the target's clothing, an uncrushed dead spider and a sewing needle worth 600+ GP, all consumed. You curse a creature with narcissistic hubris. The target makes an Intelligence save.\n\n**Successful save.** The target takes 2d10 Psychic damage and knows it was cursed.\n\n**Failed save.** The target takes 4d10 Psychic damage, has the Blinded condition for 1 minute, and is cursed.\n\n**Trigger.** The next time the target hears its name spoken, the speaker sounds derisive whatever their real tone, and the curse moves to Stage 1.\n\n**Stage 1.** It hears veiled insults everywhere and believes everyone envies its brilliance and talent.\n\n**Stage 2.** It is restless unless it is working toward a goal. It gains no benefit from a Short Rest.\n\n**Stage 3.** It believes everyone is part of a conspiracy to ruin it. Whenever it fails a D20 Test, it has Disadvantage on the next D20 Test it makes.\n\n**Culmination.** The creature twists into a deformed figure and becomes a Mind Siphon."],
"Curse of Foul Blight": ["Level 4 staged curse. Charisma save: 6d10 Necrotic and cursed on a fail, 3d10 and no healing for 1 minute on a success. Stages bring coughing, a rotting 10-ft aura and no Concentration, then healing only from Short Rest Hit Point Dice. Ends as a Plague Carrion.",
 "Unlimited range, until cured. Material cost: a shred of the target's hair or flesh, a chunk of rotten meat and a jewelry box worth 600+ GP, all consumed. You curse a creature with a putrefying, stinking pox. The target makes a Charisma save.\n\n**Successful save.** The target takes 3d10 Necrotic damage and knows it was cursed. For 1 minute it cannot gain Temporary Hit Points or regain Hit Points.\n\n**Failed save.** The target takes 6d10 Necrotic damage and is cursed.\n\n**Trigger.** The next time the target searches its garments or gear, it finds them infested with insects, and the curse moves to Stage 1.\n\n**Stage 1.** It has a minor cough and breaks into a coughing fit whenever it speaks more than a few words. This does not affect spellcasting.\n\n**Stage 2.** The stench of rot hangs around it. Within 10 feet of the creature, food and drink spoil quickly, jewelry tarnishes and wood rots. It has Disadvantage on Charisma checks and saves and cannot maintain Concentration.\n\n**Stage 3.** Its skin is covered in pockmarks, pustules and lesions, and insects swarm its clothes. It can regain Hit Points only by spending Hit Point Dice after a Short Rest.\n\n**Culmination.** The creature twists into a deformed figure and becomes a Plague Carrion."],
"Curse of Ill-Fated Fortune": ["Level 5 staged curse. Dexterity save: 7d10 Thunder and cursed on a fail, 3d10 and Disadvantage on its first D20 Test within 1 minute on a success. Stages bring bad luck, Dexterity Disadvantage, then Disadvantage on Initiative, Speed 10 ft and Prone on a missed attack. Ends as a Herald of Calamity.",
 "Unlimited range, until cured. Material cost: a discarded piece of the target's gear, a splinter of bone and a set of dice worth 800+ GP, all consumed. You curse a creature with lethal bad luck. The target makes a Dexterity save.\n\n**Successful save.** The target takes 3d10 Thunder damage and knows it was cursed. It has Disadvantage on the first D20 Test it makes in the next 1 minute.\n\n**Failed save.** The target takes 7d10 Thunder damage and is cursed.\n\n**Trigger.** The next time the target walks through a doorway, it stubs its toe or bangs its head, and the curse moves to Stage 1.\n\n**Stage 1.** Minor mishaps follow it. Shops close just as it arrives and its gear breaks at awkward moments.\n\n**Stage 2.** It becomes a beacon of bad luck, and harmless setbacks turn dangerous. Objects keep ending up in its way. It has Disadvantage on Dexterity checks and saves.\n\n**Stage 3.** It is prone to accidents, and even simple tasks have unforeseen deadly results. It has Disadvantage on Initiative checks, its Speed is reduced to 10 feet, and it has the Prone condition whenever it misses an attack roll.\n\n**Culmination.** The creature twists into a deformed figure and becomes a Herald of Calamity."],
"Curse of Insatiable Greed": ["Level 5 staged curse. Wisdom save: 6d10 Cold and Speed 0 (rising 5 ft per turn) on a fail, 4d10 on a success. Stages bring trinket stealing, Wisdom Disadvantage and a hoard, then no Reactions. Ends as a Verminous Abomination.",
 "Unlimited range, until cured. Material cost: a coin the target once owned, a rat's tail and a golden crown of thorns worth 800+ GP, all consumed. You curse a creature with bitter, self-destructive greed. The target makes a Wisdom save.\n\n**Successful save.** The target takes 4d10 Cold damage and knows it was cursed.\n\n**Failed save.** The target takes 6d10 Cold damage and its Speed is reduced to 0 for 1 minute. At the end of each of its turns, its Speed increases by 5 feet until it reaches its normal maximum. It is also cursed.\n\n**Trigger.** The next time the target finishes a Short Rest or Long Rest, it notices a valued item is missing, and the curse moves to Stage 1.\n\n**Stage 1.** It feels compelled to steal trinkets.\n\n**Stage 2.** It finds a secret place to stash stolen trinkets and grows anxious about leaving it for long. It has Disadvantage on Wisdom checks and saves.\n\n**Stage 3.** It is driven to turn its hoard into a labyrinth of possessions and treasure and wants to stay in this lair. It cannot take Reactions.\n\n**Culmination.** The creature twists into a deformed figure and becomes a Verminous Abomination."],
"Curse of Lost Sentiment": ["Level 4 staged curse. Intelligence save: 6d10 Force, Stunned until the end of its next turn and cursed on a fail, 3d10 and Incapacitated on a success. Stages bring forgetting, Intelligence Disadvantage, then no Bonus Actions. Ends as a Dream Whisperer.",
 "Unlimited range, until cured. Material cost: a lock of hair from someone the target loves, an animal's heart and an idol worth 600+ GP, all consumed. You curse a creature with lost memories and horrific madness. The target makes an Intelligence save.\n\n**Successful save.** The target takes 3d10 Force damage and has the Incapacitated condition until the end of its next turn. It does not know it was cursed.\n\n**Failed save.** The target takes 6d10 Force damage, has the Stunned condition until the end of its next turn, and is cursed.\n\n**Trigger.** The next time the target finishes a Long Rest, it has nightmares of being abandoned or left alone, and the curse moves to Stage 1.\n\n**Stage 1.** It begins forgetting events of the past few days and the names of acquaintances.\n\n**Stage 2.** It forgets everyone but its closest companions and imagines hidden threats and scheming rivals. It has Disadvantage on Intelligence checks and saves.\n\n**Stage 3.** It forgets even its closest companions, its own identity and its goals. The curse invents the delusion of a great conspiracy that only it can stop, and it feels compelled to do whatever it thinks is needed to uncover it. It cannot take Bonus Actions.\n\n**Culmination.** The creature twists into a deformed figure and becomes a Dream Whisperer."],
"Curse of Ravenous Hunger": ["Level 3 staged curse. Constitution save: 4d10 Poison, Poisoned 1 minute and cursed on a fail, 2d10 and Poisoned until the end of its next turn on a success. Stages bring hunger, Constitution Disadvantage and lower Hit Point maximum, then no Advantage on D20 Tests. Ends as a Bloated Gastromorph.",
 "Unlimited range, until cured. Material cost: a morsel of food that belonged to the target, a sun-dried slug and a dining plate worth 400+ GP, all consumed. You curse a creature with painful, unending starvation. The target makes a Constitution save.\n\n**Successful save.** The target takes 2d10 Poison damage, has the Poisoned condition until the end of its next turn, and knows it was cursed.\n\n**Failed save.** The target takes 4d10 Poison damage, has the Poisoned condition for 1 minute, and is cursed.\n\n**Trigger.** The next time it eats a meal, the creature bites its tongue and its mouth fills with blood, and the curse moves to Stage 1.\n\n**Stage 1.** It is gripped by an insatiable appetite.\n\n**Stage 2.** It feels compelled to eat unsuitable things such as coins, flowers, glass and dirt. It has Disadvantage on Constitution saves, and its Hit Point maximum decreases by its character level (or by its number of Hit Point Dice if it has no character level).\n\n**Stage 3.** It becomes ravenous and must eat Humanoid flesh, since no other food satisfies it. It cannot have Advantage on D20 Tests.\n\n**Culmination.** The creature twists into a deformed figure and becomes a Bloated Gastromorph."],
"Curse of Uncontrollable Wrath": ["Level 6 staged curse. Wisdom save: 8d10 Psychic and cursed on a fail, 4d10 and Disadvantage on Reaction attacks for 1 minute on a success. Stages bring aggression, no Short Rest benefit, then no Long Rest benefit. Ends as an Avatar of Slaughter.",
 "Unlimited range, until cured. Material cost: blood or other fluid of the target, a severed hand and a serrated knife worth 1,000+ GP, all consumed. You curse a creature with an uncontrollable temper and a lust for violence. The target makes a Wisdom save.\n\n**Successful save.** The target takes 4d10 Psychic damage and knows it was cursed. For 1 minute it has Disadvantage on attacks made with a Reaction.\n\n**Failed save.** The target takes 8d10 Psychic damage and is cursed.\n\n**Trigger.** The next time the cursed creature attacks with a weapon or casts a spell using a Spellcasting Focus, an old wound reopens and the curse moves to Stage 1.\n\n**Stage 1.** It is easily agitated and aggressive.\n\n**Stage 2.** It becomes obsessed with violence. Fighting alone thrills it and its attitude to allies sours as the curse grows. It gains no benefit from a Short Rest.\n\n**Stage 3.** It is driven by insatiable bloodlust and cannot rest while enemies remain to be slaughtered. It gains no benefit from a Long Rest.\n\n**Culmination.** The creature twists into a deformed figure and becomes an Avatar of Slaughter."],
"Dark Sacrament": ["Spend 4 Hit Point Dice. Melee spell attack with the dagger: spent dice plus 4d8 Necrotic. A kill grants a 10-minute dark blessing: Unassailable, Unbreakable or Unerring. +1d8 per slot level above 4.",
 "Self, Action. Material: a dagger encrusted in jewels worth 100+ GP. To cast this spell you must expend four Hit Point Dice, or it fails automatically. Make a melee spell attack with the Material component against a creature within 5 feet. On a hit, roll the Hit Point Dice you expended plus 4d8. You deal Necrotic damage equal to the total.\n\n**Dark blessing.** If this damage reduces the creature to 0 Hit Points, it dies at once and you gain one of these dark blessings of your choice:\n- Unassailable. You have Advantage on all saving throws.\n- Unbreakable. Your size increases by one category (Medium to Large, for example). At the start of each of your turns you gain Temporary Hit Points equal to your Constitution modifier (minimum 1). Your weapon attacks deal an extra 1d4 damage.\n- Unerring. Your Proficiency Bonus increases by 2.\n\nWhen you take Radiant damage while you have a dark blessing, you take an extra 1d4 Radiant damage. The blessing ends after 10 minutes or when you drop to 0 Hit Points, whichever comes first.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** The initial damage increases by 1d8 for each slot level above 4."],
"Dazing Blast": ["Range 60 ft. Constitution save: 2d6 Force and Stunned until the end of its next turn. On a success, damage only. +1 target per slot level above 2.",
 "Range 60 ft. A wave of force leaves your palms and strikes a creature within range. The target makes a Constitution save. On a fail it takes 2d6 Force damage and has the Stunned condition until the end of its next turn. On a success it takes the damage only.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** You can target one more creature for each slot level above 2."],
"Earth Worm": ["Range 60 ft. A worm maw lasts 1 minute. Bonus Action melee spell attack: 3d8 plus your modifier Piercing. Large or smaller targets make a Dexterity save or are swallowed (Blinded, Restrained, 6d6 Bludgeoning each of your turns).",
 "Range 60 ft, Concentration up to 1 minute. You turn the ground at an unoccupied point within range into a wormlike maw. As a Bonus Action, make a melee spell attack against a creature within 5 feet of the worm. On a hit, the target takes Piercing damage equal to 3d8 plus your spellcasting ability modifier.\n\n**Swallowing.** If the target is Large or smaller, it must succeed on a Dexterity save or be swallowed. A swallowed creature has the Blinded and Restrained conditions, has Cover against attacks and effects from outside the worm, and takes 6d6 Bludgeoning damage at the start of each of your turns.\n\n**Escaping.** A trapped creature can take an action to make a Strength (Athletics) check against your spell save DC. On a success it is spat out, has the Prone condition, and lands in an unoccupied space within 10 feet of the worm.\n\n**Moving.** As a Bonus Action, you can move the worm up to 30 feet."],
"Elemental Exhalation": ["Self (30-ft Cone). Choose Air, Coldfire, Earth, Fire or Water. Dexterity save: 5d6 damage of that type (half on success) plus a rider on a fail. +1d6 per slot level above 3.",
 "Self (30-foot Cone). When you cast this spell, choose one element. It sets the damage type and adds an effect on a failed save. Each creature in the Cone of destructive elemental energy makes a Dexterity save. On a fail it takes 5d6 damage of the chosen type. On a success it takes half as much damage only.\n- Air. Thunder damage. Each creature that fails is pushed 10 feet away from you.\n- Coldfire. Cold damage. Each creature that fails has the Frightened condition until the start of your next turn.\n- Earth. Bludgeoning damage. Each creature that fails has its Speed reduced to 0 until the end of its next turn.\n- Fire. Fire damage. Each creature that fails is set alight and takes 2d6 Fire damage at the end of its next turn. As an action it can put out the flames by giving itself the Prone condition and rolling on the ground. The fire also goes out if it is doused, submerged or suffocated.\n- Water. Acid damage. Each creature that fails has the Prone condition.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** The damage increases by 1d6 for each slot level above 3."],
"Emmeline's Essence Infusion": ["Touch. Consume a vial with 1+ ounce of blood worth 100+ GP. A nonmagical weapon becomes a magic weapon needing attunement, with a bonus set by the blood: Aberration, Celestial, Dragon, Fey or Fiend. Permanent after 1 year of attunement.",
 "Touch, lasts while you are attuned. Material: a diamond vial holding at least 1 ounce of blood, worth at least 100 GP, which the spell consumes. You target one nonmagical weapon within range. It becomes magical and gains a benefit based on the creature type of the blood used. The weapon requires Attunement and only the attuned creature gains the benefits.\n- Aberration. Your weapon attacks deal an extra 1d6 Psychic damage on a hit. You can also speak telepathically with any creature that has taken at least 1 damage from this weapon in the last 24 hours, if you are both on the same plane.\n- Celestial. Your weapon attacks deal an extra 1d6 Radiant damage on a hit. As a Bonus Action you can make the weapon shed Bright Light in a 30-foot radius and Dim Light for another 30 feet. Another Bonus Action ends the light.\n- Dragon. Your attack rolls with this weapon score a Critical Hit on a 19 or 20 on the d20. You also have Advantage on saves to avoid or end the Frightened condition.\n- Fey. Your weapon attacks deal an extra 1d4 Force damage on a hit. Once per turn, when you hit a creature within 30 feet with this weapon, you can teleport to an unoccupied space you can see within 5 feet of it.\n- Fiend. Your weapon attacks deal an extra 1d6 Necrotic damage on a hit. As a Bonus Action you can change this extra damage to Cold or Fire.\n\n**Duration.** When you cast the spell, you attune to the weapon, and the spell lasts as long as you stay attuned. During that time the item can be affected by Dispel Magic. If you stay attuned for 1 year, the enchantment becomes permanent and the spell ends."],
"Enspelled Armament": ["Self, 1 hour. Create an energy replica of a Simple or Martial weapon you are proficient with. Use your spellcasting modifier, no ammunition, thrown weapons return, damage becomes Force. +1d4 per slot level above 2.",
 "Self, 1 hour. Material: a vial of oil and water. Choose one Simple or Martial weapon. An iridescent energy copy of it appears in your hands. For the duration you are proficient with it, and when you attack with it you can use your spellcasting ability modifier for attack and damage rolls instead of Strength or Dexterity. Attacks with it need no ammunition, and if you throw it as part of a ranged attack, it returns to your hand right after the attack resolves. Its damage is Force instead of its normal type.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** The weapon's damage increases by 1d4 for each slot level above 2. With a level 5 or higher slot, the duration is 8 hours."],
"Extract Iron": ["Spend 3 Hit Point Dice. Draw pounds of iron from your blood equal to the roll and shape nonmagical metal objects of poor but working quality. More dice and iron per slot level above 3.",
 "Self. Material: a rusty knife. To cast this spell you must expend three Hit Point Dice, or it fails automatically. Roll the expended dice and draw a number of pounds of iron from your blood equal to the total. You shape this iron into nonmagical metal objects whose combined weight cannot exceed the number rolled. The objects are poor in quality but functional.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** You can expend one more Hit Point Die and create more iron for each slot level above 3."],
"Fiend Flesh": ["Touch. A willing creature gains red scales for 1 hour: Resistance to Cold, Fire and Lightning, Immunity to Poison damage. Concentration.",
 "Touch, Concentration up to 1 hour. You touch a willing creature and turn its skin to red scales. Until the spell ends, the target has Resistance to Cold, Fire and Lightning damage and Immunity to Poison damage."],
"Flash Fever": ["Range 60 ft. Constitution save: 4d6 Fire on a fail, spell ends on a success. Then 2d6 Fire at the start of each turn. Three successful saves end it, three failures deal 8d6 Fire. +1d6 initial per slot level above 3.",
 "Range 60 ft, Concentration up to 1 minute. Choose a creature you can see within range. It breaks into a cold sweat and makes a Constitution save. On a fail, the sweat becomes a burning fever and the creature takes 4d6 Fire damage. On a success, the spell ends.\n\n**Ongoing fever.** For the duration, the target takes 2d6 Fire damage at the start of each of its turns. It repeats the Constitution save at the end of each of its turns until it has three successes or three failures. Three successes end the spell. Three failures deal 8d6 Fire damage to it and end the spell.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** The initial damage increases by 1d6 for each slot level above 3."],
"Flense": ["Range 60 ft. Ranged spell attack: 8d6 Necrotic on a hit, with a Constitution save for half. Each turn, a Magic action forces another save for 8d6 (half on success). Concentration, 1 minute.",
 "Range 60 ft, Concentration up to 1 minute. Using necromantic force, you strip the skin from a creature you can see within range. Make a ranged spell attack against it. On a hit, the target takes 8d6 Necrotic damage on a failed save, or half as much on a successful one.\n\n**Repeating.** On each of your turns until the spell ends, you can take a Magic action to make the same target take a Constitution save. It takes 8d6 Necrotic damage on a fail, or half as much on a success.\n\n**Ending.** The spell ends if the target moves out of range, is reduced to 0 Hit Points, or you can no longer see it."],
"Fleshcrawl": ["Range 100 ft. Constitution save: 8d10 Necrotic (half on success). The flayed skin rises as an allied Fleshling Construct that shares your Initiative and acts right after you. Concentration, 1 minute.",
 "Range 100 ft, Concentration up to 1 minute. You rip the flesh from a creature and shape it into a twisted mass of blood and skin that attacks that creature. A creature you can see within range makes a Constitution save. On a fail it takes 8d10 Necrotic damage, and its flayed skin is animated as a grotesque copy using the Fleshling Construct stat block. On a success it takes half as much damage only.\n\n**The fleshling.** It is an ally to you and your allies. In combat it shares your Initiative count but takes its turn right after yours. It obeys your verbal commands (no action needed from you). If you give none, it takes the Dodge action and uses its movement to avoid danger. It disappears when it drops to 0 Hit Points or the spell ends.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** Use the slot's level as the spell level in the stat block."],
"Frightful Start": ["Cantrip. Range 30 ft. The target succeeds on a Wisdom save or has the Frightened condition until the start of your next turn.",
 "Range 30 ft, 1 round. You twist your face to scare a creature you can see within range. The creature must succeed on a Wisdom save or have the Frightened condition until the start of your next turn."],
"Ghost Light": ["Touch an object up to 10 ft across. It sheds silvery Bright Light in 20 ft and Dim Light 20 ft more, visible only to creatures you named within 10 ft. 1 hour.",
 "Touch, 1 hour. You touch one object no larger than 10 feet in any dimension and name any number of creatures you can see within 10 feet. Until the spell ends, the object sheds silvery Bright Light in a 20-foot radius and Dim Light for another 20 feet. Only the creatures you named when casting can see this light. Everyone else sees the area as they normally would."],
"Greater Animate Dead": ["Range 10 ft. Raise up to 5 Undead of CR 2 or lower from corpses. Command them as a Bonus Action within 120 ft. Control lasts 24 hours and can be renewed on up to four creatures. +1 Undead per slot level above 5.",
 "Range 10 ft. Material: a drop of blood, a piece of flesh, a pinch of bone dust and a black onyx stone worth 75+ GP for each level of CR you animate. Choose corpses within range. You can reanimate up to 5 Undead creatures of Challenge Rating 2 or lower from them.\n\n**Commanding.** On each of your turns you can take a Bonus Action to mentally command any creature made with this spell that is within 120 feet of you. With several creatures you can command any or all of them and give each the same order. You decide its action and movement for its next turn, or you can give a general order such as guarding a room or corridor. With no orders, it only defends itself against hostile creatures. Once given an order, it follows it until the task is done.\n\n**Control.** The creature is under your control for 24 hours, then stops obeying you. To keep control for another 24 hours, you must cast this spell on it again before the current period ends. This use reasserts control over up to four creatures you animated with this spell rather than animating a new one, and it needs no components with a GP cost.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** You can animate one more Undead creature for each slot level above 5."],
"Heartseeker": ["Spend 6 Hit Point Dice. Range 300 ft. Ranged spell attack: Piercing damage equal to a roll of the spent dice. The first hit on the target each round after its turn is a Critical Hit. Constitution save each turn end, 3d8 Necrotic on success ends it. Concentration, 1 minute.",
 "Range 300 ft, Concentration up to 1 minute. Material: a ruby worth 100+ GP. To cast this spell you must expend six Hit Point Dice, or it fails automatically. Your blood flows out and crystallizes into a barbed arrow that you fire at a creature. Make a ranged spell attack against a target within range. On a hit, roll the Hit Point Dice you expended. The creature takes Piercing damage equal to the total.\n\n**Burrowing arrow.** The arrow stays lodged and burrows toward the creature's heart, leaving it open to injury. Until the spell ends, the first successful attack against the creature after its turn ends each round is automatically a Critical Hit.\n\n**Saves.** The target makes a Constitution save at the end of each of its turns. On a fail the effect continues. On a success the creature takes 3d8 Necrotic damage and the spell ends."],
"Holy Word": ["Cantrip. Range 60 ft. Ranged spell attack: 1d8 Radiant. Fey, Fiend or Undead also lose 10 ft of Speed and cannot take Reactions until the end of their next turn. Damage 2d8 at level 5, 3d8 at 11, 4d8 at 17.",
 "Range 60 ft. You whisper a divine word, careful not to speak loudly, since such celestial power is not for the unworthy. Make a ranged spell attack against a target within range. On a hit, the target takes 1d8 Radiant damage. If the target is a Fey, Fiend or Undead, its Speed is also reduced by 10 feet and it cannot take Reactions until the end of its next turn.\n\n**Cantrip Upgrade.** The damage increases by 1d8 at levels 5 (2d8), 11 (3d8) and 17 (4d8)."],
"Hunter Sense": ["Cantrip. Touch a willing creature. For 1 minute, when it makes a Wisdom (Perception) check, a d20 roll of 9 or lower counts as 10. Concentration.",
 "Touch, Concentration up to 1 minute. You touch a willing creature and sharpen its senses. For the duration, whenever the target makes a Wisdom (Perception) check, it can treat a d20 roll of 9 or lower as a 10."],
}
